    "title": "interfaces: `findAncestorByHash` returns true for an unknown descendant",
    "body": "### Is there an existing issue for this?\n\n- [x] I have searched the existing issues\n\n### Current behaviour\n\nWhile testing an external python capnp ipc client on regtest, I found that `findAncestorByHash` returns success for an unknown descendant hash when the ancestor is known. I also reproduced this directly on `master`.\n\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\n`findAncestorByHash` should return `false` when the descendant hash is unknown\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nAdd this to the existing `findAncestorByHash` test in `src/test/interfaces_tests.cpp` to reproduce the issue\n\n```cpp\nBOOST_CHECK(!chain->findAncestorByHash(uint256{}, active[0]->GetBlockHash()));\n```\nand then running\n```\ncmake --build build --target test_bitcoin -j8 && ./build/bin/test_bitcoin --run_test=interfaces_tests/findAncestorByHash\n```\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n```\ntest/interfaces_tests.cpp:97: error: in \"interfaces_tests/findAncestorByHash\": check !chain->findAncestorByHash(uint256{}, active[0]->GetBlockHash()) has failed\n```\n\n### How did you obtain Bitcoin Core\n\nCompiled from source\n\n### What version of Bitcoin Core are you using?\n\nv31.1\n\n### Operating system and version\n\nMacOS 27.0.1 arm\n\n### Machine specifications\n\n_No response_",
